1179) (HhTs) ac: Divide co: Tent Wall ab: ?: The pictograph is a picture of a wall. The is a picture of a man laying on his side. Combined these mean "wall of sides". The tent wall divides or separates the inside from the outside. The wall inside the tent divides the tent into two sections.
fm) (Hh-TsY) - Arrow: As dividing flesh. [freq. 3] |kjv: arrow| {H2686}
V) (Hh-TsTs) - Divide: A division of something or a band as a division. [freq. 3] (vf: Paal, Pual, Piel, Participle) |kjv: band, archer, midst| {H2686}
